                        <field name="dc_title">The Hon. Mr. Acting Secretary of the Office of Grace and Justice,..., tells me what follows [Printed Text]: "Hon. Mr. Having represented to the King our Lord the governmental Upper Board of Surgery that despite the fact that, according to what is prevented in art.° 5, cap.° 18 of the ordinances of the said Faculty inserted in Real cédula 6 de Mayo, 1804, directs exhorts to the Justicias of the peoples to prevent the egercicio of the Surgery or of any of its bouquets to those that lack the respective approval titles,... </field>
